</TABLE></DIV> <P STYLE="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-left:9%; font-size:11pt; font-family:ARIAL" ALIGN="justify">The initial carrying amount of the financial liability was determined by discounting the estimated
future interest and principal payments at a discount rate of 15%. </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-left:9%; font-size:11pt; font-family:ARIAL" ALIGN="justify">The carrying amounts of the equity component (the warrants) was
established using the residual fair value approach, which takes the difference between the principal amount received from the Credit Facility (US$6,000,000) less the fair value of the loan. The value of the warrants of $539,266 (US$380,553), net of
financing cost of $6,299 (US$4,445) is recorded within warrant reserves on the statement of financial position. </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-left:9%; font-size:11pt; font-family:ARIAL" ALIGN="justify">The carrying value
of the loans will be accreted using the effective interest rate method over the term of the Credit Facility. The effective interest rate for the 2023 tranche and 2025 tranche is estimated at 23.74% and 15.10%, respectively. </P>
<P STYLE="font-size:12pt; margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt">&nbsp;</P>
